{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T11:45:41.411Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4400fc26dce6d999aa811cc5","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-27T11:45:41.408Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Behavioral revert proof in disposable copies: disabling the source guard or removing its apply and repeat workflow arguments each failed the source-drift regression. Removing either recovery fence replayed a pending plan and failed the rejection check. Reverting the annotation receipt, dependency receipt, plain type comparison or Projects no-op comparison each failed its targeted assertion. Restoring the released comment read/append function in the candidate on the frozen pm-rl caller again produced 17 → 18 → 19 comments and appended a history row. Reverting only the reader stayed byte-identical for unchanged text because native ifAbsent still deduplicated. The caller SDK projected the legacy 1,221-character comment as 253 characters and dropped its marker. The fixed linked test command passed 7/7."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T11:45:41.411Z"}],"before_hash":"65495ffb57240981ca48a5a8deae7e01ebfdcc870d823e0c6ea4c3909afc7bac","after_hash":"26996964bfa0b18723f80e70e218cfef9a89ceee96194109453b4b47fc8fe5d8","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"3580d495b